# PROJECT: FITLIFE AI — COMPLETE AI-POWERED FITNESS WEBSITE FRONTEND

Act as a senior UI/UX designer, frontend architect, React developer and product designer.

Build a complete, premium-quality, responsive web application named **FitLife AI**. It is an AI-powered fitness platform that helps users exercise with camera-based movement guidance, follow personalized workout and diet plans, track daily habits, and understand their fitness progress.

I want a fully designed and navigable application, not merely a landing page, wireframe, static mockup or collection of disconnected screens.

The application should have a consistent design system, reusable components, functional navigation, realistic interactions, well-organized code and a clear path to future backend integration.

## CRITICAL PROJECT AND FILE RULES

1. First inspect the existing workspace and identify its framework, dependencies, source directories and current files.
2. If a project already exists, continue inside that same project. Do not initialize a second application or create a nested project folder.
3. Preserve all existing working code and configuration unless a change is genuinely necessary.
4. If the workspace is empty, initialize a single frontend application using React, TypeScript and the framework supported by the environment.
5. Use the existing routing and styling approach when possible.
6. Do not create duplicate components, duplicate package files, unnecessary configuration files or another independent frontend.
7. Do not overwrite package.json, lockfiles, environment files or framework configuration blindly.
8. Keep components modular so authentication, the AI engine, database and APIs can be added later.
9. Do not expose API keys, service-role credentials or private secrets in browser code.
10. Implement the frontend now. Do not pretend that an external AI service, authentication provider, database or live pose detection is connected unless it has actually been implemented and tested.

